data/: the cartridge's data as typed tables (plan section 3). Places live
only in the .c files here, behind data_internal.h. Checked by
tools/data_check.py ROM (every range against the ROM, every reader against a
second reading of the ROM, no ROM place in game code outside data/;
PLANT=1 shows it can fail).

Who writes what (the master's work split, 2026-11-19; PLAN.md "Files"):
  stage 2's: data.c, data.h, data_internal.h, the shared formats below, the checks
  each area's: data/<area>_tables.{c,h}, written when it converts the reading routine

Shared formats (stage 2's), 2026-11-19:
  sound_lists.c   the 55-entry upload table at $85:8000 and its lists (42 used: config/aladdin/spclists.csv)
  graphics.c      the palette loads ($84:C000, 98); the packed-graphics format; the level graphics
                  lists ($80:DF98, 66 levels); the unpack sets ($80:F039, 50); the animation
                  sets' graphics ($82:AC18/$82:AC58, sets 32 up)
  level_maps.c    the level maps: headers ($80:E3DC, 66), block lists and tiles, layouts ($80:E460, 66)
Area tables written here before the split, now their areas':
  video_tables.c  the quarter sine ($82:87D4, 64 steps)       -> video
  input_tables.c  the demos' pad scripts ($84:F700)           -> input (stage 6)

Code the game reads as a table: being settled (the 8,972 S-CPU code bytes the
traces read as data); cart.dat leaves all code out until it lands.

AnimSetGraphicsUnpack's entries at $82:AC18 + set * 2: the traces read them
only for sets 32 and up, at $82:AC58 on (data); the words for sets 0-31
would be code bytes no trace reads.

Record comment found wrong (a note only; the record is not edited from the
native work): video/unpack.c's LEVEL_GFX says bank $81; LevelGraphicsLoad runs
with DB = $80 and the table is $80:DF98.
